    "turn_text": "Thank you very much, Senator. To come, I'm from the Voice of America Russian Service. My question is, after recent Russian Ukrainian prisoners swoop, It seems that some politicians, at least in Europe, attempted to have business as usual with Russia, like President Macron of France, ascending his foreign minister of defence for talks. And actually President Trump is talking about possible invitation for Mr. Putin for G7 next year. What do you think about such an invitation if it will be extended? And if you're critical to it, what tools Congress has to kind of limit the possibility of it? Thank you very",
