    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Thank you very much. I don't think that they should be led into the G7, both because of Ukraine, but also because of this. It is, say the least, unfortunate that we have a president who still isn't admitting really that this happened, who stood on a stage next to Putin in Helsinki and said, I don't see any reason why he would lie about it, about Putin. taking his view instead of the view of the intelligence agencies in the United States. We now have a bipartisan report that's been released by the Intelligence Committee on which I served. It makes it very clear that this happened and who did it and that it was sustained and that it was real. And then that didn't stop the president from going to Japan and making a joke about it. And furthermore, I know having spent time with a number of leaders from Western Europe, how worried they are about our absence of leadership on this topic. They know they can't defend themselves against Russia. They're very worried about the way Russia is inciting right-wing groups through the same kind of thing. By the way, I didn't show you any of these. Should I show just a few of these slides? And so we've got to provide more leadership. I would say, Vivek, do you want to, does that work or no? What Congress can do, I think, to stop this is what we should do as an administration, if we had a White House with somebody who would take this seriously, is we should be sanctioning Russia for doing this. using our own measures that are equivalent, not identical, but to push back on what they've done, so that they know that there's a penalty for doing it. And we should be leading our European allies in their fight against this as well. I think that's what we should be doing. And Congress wants to pass, not all of Congress, obviously, but we have bipartisan legislation in the Congress that would do things like shore up our election infrastructure at the local level against this kind of attack. It would require campaigns to notify the FBI if they'd had this sort of interaction with the Russians. And Mitch McConnell won't put it on the floor. It's bipartisan. I'd love to see which United States Senator doesn't want to vote for this election protection legislation. I'd love to see it. which is why we should have a debate. This is one of my favorite ones. This is NASCAR Jesus, given to you by the Russians. It has the NASCAR sign, and Jesus holding it a cell weapon in one hand and a mountain dew in the other hand. This is a series of... And this is, there are a whole series of these that were targeted to suppress the African-American vote all over America. You know, the Russians, they didn't care. They were on every side of every issue. So you'll see ones where they are supporting Black Lives Matter. And then you'll see others where they're taking the police department's view. All they care about is fomenting the divisions and the dissensions. This is based on a real op, and by the way, as those of you that are historians know, the Russians have been unbelievable propagandists from time immemorial, and this is a really stunning piece of propaganda, I think, that was based on an op-ed piece that ran in the New York Times. This you may not have known, no, yeah, did you know Nobel Peace Prize winner President Barack Obama dropped over 23,000 bombs on majority Muslim countries. Most of what they ran was anti-Muslim, anti-Islam stuff, but they ran things like this, too. Thanks.",
